SUMMARY:Europe\, Germany and Heilbronn: A historical and cultural journey 
 of discovery
DESCRIPTION:Join this self-paced course and get acquainted with your new h
 ome in Heilbronn! Register here!\nStudents will explore a completely digit
 al self-study path\, which can be completed independently in preparation f
 or their stay. The module is designed for a total of 33-40 semester hours 
 per week. \nLearning objectives:The module aims to prepare foreign studen
 ts for their stay in Germany and to encourage their anticipation. After co
 mpleting the module\, students should:1.Have a basic knowledge of German h
 istory and understand its influence on today's society.2.Recognize and ref
 lect on Germany's cultural characteristics and values.3.Have a basic under
 standing of German political systems and institutions.4.Acquire specific k
 nowledge about the Heilbronn region and understand its historical\, cultur
 al and economic significance.\nContents:Week 1: Political history of Europ
 e\, Germany and Heilbronn - developments and influences-German history fro
 m the Middle Ages through the Weimar Republic to the present day-Overview 
 of the political systems and developments in Europe and Germany-Introducti
 on to the European Union and its institutions-Bonus material: Heilbronn's 
 role in regional political contexts\nWeek 2: Economic development in Europ
 e\, Germany and Heilbronn - changes and innovations-Industrial revolution 
 in Europe and Germany-Economic recovery after the Second World War: German
 y and Heilbronn-Influence of European economic policy on local companies-B
 onus material: Heilbronn as innovation and business location (e.g. viticul
 ture\, mechanical engineering)\, virtual excursion / presentation to a lea
 ding company in Heilbronn\nWeek 3: Social and cultural developments - soci
 al structures and cultural diversity-Social movements in Europe and German
 y-Integration and migration in Germany and cultural diversity-Emergence an
 d origin of German culture and values-Bonus material: Local traditions and
  cultural events in Heilbronn\nWeek 4: Technological developments and inno
 vations - in Europe\, Germany and Heilbronn-Technological milestones in Eu
 rope and Germany-Meaning of the "Made in Germany" label and its origin and
  development-Examples of successful start-ups and innovation centers in Ge
 rmany-Bonus material: Heilbronn's role as a location for research and deve
 lopment and developments over the last 10 years\nWeek 5: Environmental and
  sustainability issues-Environmental movements in Europe and Germany-Legis
 lation to change sustainability activities in Europe and Germany-Environme
 ntal facts about Europe and Germany compared to other countries (e.g. Chin
 a\, USA)-Bonus material: Projects and programs to promote and protect the 
 environment in Heilbronn\nWeek 6: Legal framework and social norms-Origin 
 and overview of the German legal system-European law and its impact on Ger
 many-Bonus material: Living together in Heilbronn\nPlease note that TUM st
 udents do not receive ECTS credit for this course.
